## Research order and scope
The formerly missing genuine **S1E03 — Raw End Of Joke Stick** has been recovered and analyzed at the proper episode ID, connecting the S1E02 guild return to S1E04's grick cliffhanger. **Season One / first arc completed through S1E12 — End Friends**. [Eight-chapter first-arc narrative](narrative/SEASON_ONE_ARC.md). **S2E00 — Cassius at the Guild is now classified**: a narrated in-universe cutaway simultaneous with the Season One kuo-toa mission, explicitly followed by the Season One finale announcement. **S2E01 — Very Snakey is now researched as the Season Two premiere**: the accepted Snake Island journey is mostly recovered through memory shards, with a two-week gap and return payment; the party then deals with personal/family revelations and defeats a hag at Krandal's deeded Potato Grove. [Dossier](episodes/S2E01.md). **S2E02 — Why Palor When you Can Pay Later now researched** as played Hooper–Goodwine **Wight Wedding**; guest wizard recovers **Deck of Many Things**, wight defeated and buried, wedding proceeds. [Dossier](episodes/S2E02.md). **S2E03 — Pokey Stick Junior researched**: city bulette slain, chamber under Withers Estate found and reported, **Cassius confirmed as funder of off-books Cloven reconnaissance**, **Evelyn Blackwood corrected**, farm planted, 9:30 p.m. heist not yet performed. [Dossier](episodes/S2E03.md). **S2E04 — Cover The Faces of Maces now researched** as the **completed Withers Estate burglary and escape**, with four elemental guardians and guest Shrugs (Brian Dunaway); [dossier](episodes/S2E04.md), [ASR comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E04_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E05 — Shut up, Fruit Loops! researched**: Brotherhood settles loot and postpones debrief; [dossier](episodes/S2E05.md), [comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E05_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E06 — Frog Man Cometh researched**: Koh uncovers map, party debriefs Carrie/Cassius, takes Gemholm slaad assignment and kills first transformed foe; [dossier](episodes/S2E06.md), [comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E06_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E07 — The Devils Eggs researched**: infected workers' diaries and experimental chaos reagents uncovered, Church cured, Ambermoor captured alive, black slaad specimen killed and Delvers stop with prisoner at Krandal farm; [dossier](episodes/S2E07.md), [comparison](../reports/DELVERS_S2E07_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E08 — Golden Potato Sword researched**: GM retrospectively places Ambermoor in guild cells; new guest silver-rank **Marsh** joins Chath Peak dragon mission, Skoogie grants **Arrow of Dragon Slaying**, Evelyn forges **Dragon Slayer's Longsword**, battle **paused with dragon still alive**; [dossier](episodes/S2E08.md), [ASR report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E08_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E09 — Potatopia researched**: opening retrospective resolves Fredoroth dragon hunt and loot, mental links identify Khalazar wedding pressure, Krandal feeds stranger and names skull Chad, and Wildfire recommends silver then privately confronts Evelyn about Withers; [dossier](episodes/S2E09.md), [ASR report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E09_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E10 — Carrie On researched:** actual guild lecture (Dolbluth, Khalazar, Hereditary Drone), **Remove Curse frees Anthela** and she **wakes in physical guild lab**; at the **S2E10 cutoff Evelyn hands physical red shard to Carrie**, but **S2E11 re-produces it with no shown return**, no confirmed villain death; [dossier](episodes/S2E10.md) · [ASR report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E10_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E11 — New High Score researched**: approved Silver League, official hero names/three exam scores, Maynard reports all five temple patients awake, Krandal hires Gleepo, Anthela/child reunion, Evelyn's luminous locator ribbon and unresolved shard custody discrepancy; [dossier](episodes/S2E11.md) · [ASR report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E11_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **S2E12 — The Bell of The Ball NOW RESEARCHED:** played Bronze Ball, Withers/Broscale statement, dark possession, true active Drone beneath banquet hall, **WITHERS+WILDFIRE FALL UNDERGROUND**, physical table barricade fails to stop attraction; [dossier](episodes/S2E12.md) · [ASR report](../reports/DELVERS_S2E12_ASR_COMPARISON_2026-10-25.md). **Season Two AND SECOND STORY ARC END AT S2E12** by archive owner. **Next S3E01 — Maximize The Yield**, inventoried [here](SOURCE_INVENTORY.md), **unresearched**; no invented third-arc boundary or achieved future expedition. **S1E11** resolves S1E10's submerged cutoff: the party finds further Dawnless Dunes ruins and artifacts, surfaces safely, and later **departs the kuo-toa village toward guild with three living prisoners** after an ambush, without reaching guild. The darkmantle-cowled rider escapes with the fish wizard's conch staff. **S1E10** ends underwater with a captive; that prior cutoff remains historically correct. **S1E09** resolves the cube confrontation, brings the party back for the temple's second hidden shaft and twin unresponsive elves, and ends before the newly selected kuo-toa journey. S1E05 continues the completed grick assignment, advances the party to level three and approves bronze promotion; **S1E06 actually awards the badges and completes Skull Keep**; **S1E07 documents continuing creature incursions and sends the party back to an uninspected southwestern well**. Enzo's attributed Dawnless Dunes warning remains unresolved. The older misnamed S1E03 files remain preserved as actual S1E04 copies, and the corrected MP3 has not been listened to.

Delvers needs the same kinds of documentation as Wastes: source-first dossiers, a subject-centered world reference, a continuity ledger and chronology, and readable narrative histories. The [plan](DOCUMENTATION_PLAN.md) assigns those layers their own paths and criteria for creation. No Wastes arc numbering, character pages or timeline entries carry over. Season One concludes the **first Delvers arc** at S1E12, as designated by the archive owner and supported by the episode's explicit finale. Other seasons/arcs require their own research before boundaries are asserted.

## Evidence boundary

The [guild-guide provenance register](../reports/DISCORD_SPELLING_2026-10-21.md) supplies Delvers setting-handout leads, not a played opening scene. Treat handout/planning material, played scenes, character testimony and retrospective cast commentary as distinct evidence. Future-season sources may be inventoried now without importing their revelations into an earlier episode's knowledge or spoiler horizon.

